M226 million. Concurrently, the company proposed a RM125.4 million private placement to raise working capital and a dividend reinvestment plan. The company also continued to see Warrant A conversions and has released its 2026 annual report and notice of the 43rd AGM.","notable_en":["Wholly-owned subsidiary Blossom Hectares entered into a conditional call option agreement with related party Iconic Insight to acquire 32 floors of strata space of a 4-star hotel building in Empire City, Damansara for RM226 million.","The company proposed a RM125.4 million private placement to raise working capital.","The company proposed a dividend reinvestment plan."],"risks_en":["The proposed RM125.4 million private placement may dilute existing shareholders' equity.","The proposed hotel acquisition is a related party transaction and involves a property under construction, subject to conditions of the call option and sale and purchase agreement.","The company continues to see Warrant A conversions, leading to a gradual increase in issued share capital."],"earnings_en":"For the period ended 30 June 2026, revenue was RM101.062 million and net income was RM12.559 million, with a net margin of 12.4%. Revenue grew 35.9% QoQ and net income rose 8.4% QoQ; revenue increased 46.3% YoY and net income grew 13.5% YoY."}